# pfSense Firewall Setup

## Overview
Deployed pfSense as the central firewall/router for a home lab environment to enable segmentation, DHCP, and controlled routing.

---

## Network Architecture

Internet → ISP Gateway → pfSense → Switch → Lab Devices

- WAN: DHCP (private IP from ISP)
- LAN: 192.168.50.1/24
- Internal Network: 192.168.50.0/24

---

## Hardware

- Small form factor PC (pfSense host)
- Managed switch
- Patch panel
- ISP gateway
- USB-to-Ethernet adapter

---

## Configuration Summary

### Interfaces
- WAN: connected to ISP gateway
- LAN: connected to internal switch

### LAN Setup
- Gateway: 192.168.50.1
- DHCP enabled
- Range: 192.168.50.10 – 192.168.50.100

### WAN Setup
- DHCP (default)

### DNS
- Configured external resolvers
- Disabled upstream override

### Time
- Configured NTP server
- Set correct timezone

### Security
- Default credentials changed
- Web UI secured via HTTPS

---

## Validation

- Web UI accessible via LAN gateway IP
- DHCP assigns addresses to clients
- Internet access confirmed through firewall

---

## Key Skills

- Firewall deployment
- Network segmentation
- DHCP + DNS configuration
- Routing & NAT
- Infrastructure troubleshooting

---

## Notes

- Uses single NIC + USB adapter setup
- Running behind ISP gateway (double NAT)
- Designed for scalability

